      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T16:56:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why the opposition to `optional` exactly? It\u0027s all test code, so there really isn\u0027t a code-size reason to avoid it, and it makes sense in the given context. IMO it\u0027s cleaner than having your backend-lookup function nuke the entire process.\n\nI had considered adding a `kUnsupported` enum value, but the amount of touchpoints that this would affect is much much larger than an optional (we switch on backend type a lot), and that\u0027s functionally the same as an optional IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "75e99e17_aff4789f",
      "revId": "0f7e73250832d990012612bcb6a99eff90dee567",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
